  "1067": [
    {
      "author": "non-Jedi",
      "date": "2017-11-15",
      "body": "Where is the google-doc for this? I don't understand how the mention pills relate to the spec. I'm also in general opposed to including matrix.to in any way in the spec.",
      "url": "https://github.com/matrix-org/matrix-spec-proposals/issues/1067#issuecomment-344461949"
    },
    {
      "author": "jevolk",
      "date": "2017-11-15",
      "body": "https://docs.google.com/document/d/1oRhw3DJhbVAKkHAEgyt6ccV82wtXR_11qY7JqMcesUU/?usp=sharing",
      "url": "https://github.com/matrix-org/matrix-spec-proposals/issues/1067#issuecomment-344471941"
    },
    {
      "author": "ara4n",
      "date": "2017-11-15",
      "body": "@non-Jedi - I think you are misunderstanding how matrix.to is being used here.  It is very much as an namespace (like an xmlns), so that clients which are aware of it can treat it like a URI scheme.  Clients which are *not* aware of it will treat it like a dumb URI and fall through to the matrix.to webapp itself (which is provided by matrix.org for the benefit of the whole Matrix ecosystem) but it **does not form a hard dependency on the matrix.to service whatsoever. it is just an arbitrary opaque namespace, similar to matrix:// or mx:// URLs or whatever, but one which happens for convenience to fall through to a real endpoint for stupid clients or users.**.",
      "url": "https://github.com/matrix-org/matrix-spec-proposals/issues/1067#issuecomment-344634986"
    },
    {
      "author": "non-Jedi",
      "date": "2017-11-16",
      "body": "@ara4n I did understand; I just disagree with the decision, and I hope it\r\nhasn't been made yet so that I might convince you of my point of view.\r\n\r\nMy contention is that no part of a protocol that's intentionally federated\r\nshould be linked to any singleton that can be controlled. While I realize\r\nthat it is being used as a namespace primarily, in its plain reading, a\r\nmatrix.to URL is a URL, and you admit that the reason matrix.to was chosen\r\nwas so that it could be used as a URL by \"dumb\" clients. While the URL is\r\ncontrolled by an entity that I trust right now, there is no guarantee that\r\nit will continue to be so in the future. Tbh, I'm not all that concerned\r\nabout an attacker controlling matrix.to; I'm concerned about matrix\r\nmaintaining the principle of federation: there are no privileged servers.\r\nWhile matrix.to is not a *matrix* server, if it's included in the spec, it\r\nwill still be a privileged server.\r\n\r\nI am completely fine with matrix.to being used as a de-facto namespace. I\r\nstrongly disagree with such behavior being part of the spec.\r\n",
      "url": "https://github.com/matrix-org/matrix-spec-proposals/issues/1067#issuecomment-344775521"
    },
    {
      "author": "non-Jedi",
      "date": "2017-11-16",
      "body": "Thanks @jevolk. I had seen that doc before but somehow assumed it was a Riot design doc rather than a spec proposal.",
      "url": "https://github.com/matrix-org/matrix-spec-proposals/issues/1067#issuecomment-344775805"
    }
  ],
