      "author": "bleonard252",
      "date": "2023-01-30",
      "body": "How about *m.default*? Considering it would be present in almost every message, usable on its own, and as a fallback. Otherwise I second *m.text*, as it's concise and signifies it isn't intended for use for, say, images (unless it is?)\n\nJan 30, 2023 14:06:40 Travis Ralston ***@***.***>:\n\n> ***@***.**** commented on this pull request.\n> \n> ----------------------------------------\n> \n> In proposals/1767-extensible-events.md[https://github.com/matrix-org/matrix-spec-proposals/pull/1767#discussion_r1091034149]:\n> \n>> +a minimum, a `m.markup` content block:\n> +\n> +```json5\n> +{\n> +    // irrelevant fields not shown\n> +    \"type\": \"m.message\",\n> +    \"content\": {\n> +        \"m.markup\": [\n> +            { \"body\": \"<i>Hello world</i>\", \"mimetype\": \"text/html\" },\n> +            { \"body\": \"Hello world\" }\n> +        ]\n> +    }\n> +}\n> +```\n> +\n> +`m.markup` has the following definitions associated with it:\n> \n> *m.text_block* (it really should be a text block from the layout perspective)\n> \n> they're all blocks :p\n> \n> —\n> Reply to this email directly, view it on GitHub[https://github.com/matrix-org/matrix-spec-proposals/pull/1767#discussion_r1091034149], or unsubscribe[https://github.com/notifications/unsubscribe-auth/ADUJCOTR5DUY26QIRNRS5FDWVAGL7ANCNFSM4GMYH3LQ].\n> You are receiving this because you are subscribed to this thread.[Tracking image][https://github.com/notifications/beacon/ADUJCOX3OA56OUN72VFJCEDWVAGL7A5CNFSM4GMYH3L2YY3PNVWWK3TUL52HS4DFWFIHK3DMKJSXC5LFON2FEZLWNFSXPKTDN5WW2ZLOORPWSZGOJQFQRLA.gif]\n> \n",
