      "body": "Please comment such things in a thread. But in general I don't see, why this explicitly should support e2ee. You can already send encrypted stickers (although the media itself wouldn't be encrypted, just the sticker event). But none has any idea yet how to do encrypted state events or how to encrypt this in account data (maybe SSSS?). I don't see why this MSC specifically would be blocked by that. The only thing the user leaks is which sticker packs they use and if they upload a pack in a room, the pack is available unencrypted. This is the same as the room topic, room name, room membership, room avatar, etc. Those 4 are much more critical than what sticker packs you created, especially since people will probably subscribe to public packs more often than create private packs that shouldn't be seen by the server operators.\r\n\r\nI don't see why stickers of all things should be blocked behind E2EE state events.",
