      "author": "ara4n",
      "date": "2021-07-12",
      "body": "This is an excellent MSC imo, and i would be very glad to approve for FCP once we have resolved the two final concerns, which are I think:\r\n\r\n@mscbot concern Need to [define better error codes](https://github.com/matrix-org/matrix-doc/pull/3083#pullrequestreview-704557174) to be clearer what's happening when joins fail, to let users/clients/servers know how to react.\r\n@mscbot concern Need to add the [details of the server (or user?) who granted a given join](https://github.com/matrix-org/matrix-doc/pull/3083#discussion_r665167397), so implementations can auth it more easily.  For a normal invite this would be the inviter, but we need an equivalent for this use case.\r\n\r\n<del>I also have a soft-concern that `allowed` would be a better name for the join_rule rather than `restricted`, but not going to block on that.</del>. I [changed my mind](https://github.com/matrix-org/matrix-doc/pull/3083/files#r668859320) on this (again). ",
