  "3811": [
    {
      "author": "slipeer",
      "date": "2018-12-17",
      "body": "[ICAP](https://tools.ietf.org/html/rfc3507) protocol is a standard for integrating security systems. Many antiviruses and DLP systems support it. Opensource antivirus [ClamAV](https://www.clamav.net/) can be integrated through ICAP by [C-ICAP](http://c-icap.sourceforge.net/)",
      "url": "https://github.com/matrix-org/matrix-spec-proposals/issues/3811#issuecomment-1121548942"
    },
    {
      "author": "ara4n",
      "date": "2019-01-06",
      "body": "yup, the proposal here will implement ICAP.\r\n\r\nSomeone needs to port the https://github.com/matrix-org/matrix-content-scanner#api doc into an MSC to flesh this out.",
      "url": "https://github.com/matrix-org/matrix-spec-proposals/issues/3811#issuecomment-1121548954"
    },
    {
      "author": "slipeer",
      "date": "2019-01-09",
      "body": "Note that if you implement the check when downloading a file:\r\n- download requests are always more frequent - there will be more load\r\n+ you can check the files uploaded by other servers\r\n\r\nbut if you perform file check on upload:\r\n+ in addition to the antivirus, you can integrate, for example, a DLP system.\r\n+ it is possible to block uploading and distribution of a virus file over the Matrix network.",
      "url": "https://github.com/matrix-org/matrix-spec-proposals/issues/3811#issuecomment-1121548963"
    },
    {
      "author": "ankar84",
      "date": "2021-10-18",
      "body": "> but if you perform file check on upload:\r\n> \r\n> * in addition to the antivirus, you can integrate, for example, a DLP system.\r\n> * it is possible to block uploading and distribution of a virus file over the Matrix network.\r\n\r\nI think it is the best approach of DLP and Antivirus software because Matrix stay clean in that case. Bad file don't event uploaded.",
      "url": "https://github.com/matrix-org/matrix-spec-proposals/issues/3811#issuecomment-1121548981"
    },
    {
      "author": "MTRNord",
      "date": "2022-05-10",
      "body": "> > but if you perform file check on upload:\n> > \n> > * in addition to the antivirus, you can integrate, for example, a DLP system.\n> > * it is possible to block uploading and distribution of a virus file over the Matrix network.\n> \n> I think it is the best approach of DLP and Antivirus software because Matrix stay clean in that case. Bad file don't event uploaded.\n\nWell a hostile user then would simply disable the upload checks",
      "url": "https://github.com/matrix-org/matrix-spec-proposals/issues/3811#issuecomment-1122077269"
    },
    {
      "author": "minecraftchest1",
      "date": "2022-06-20",
      "body": "I personally think the best system would be a combination of both. Scan media during upload, as well as scanning files before serving. Store a list of mxc's and/or hashes of passed/failed media to prevent constant rescanning.",
      "url": "https://github.com/matrix-org/matrix-spec-proposals/issues/3811#issuecomment-1159896862"
    },
    {
      "author": "m00nwtchr",
      "date": "2022-09-04",
      "body": "Or scan files on upload, and on retrieve when requested by the local homeserver from a remote (on the local homeserver).\r\nThough I suppose this wouldn't cover that homeserver's own users, then (in the case of a admin disabling the check).",
      "url": "https://github.com/matrix-org/matrix-spec-proposals/issues/3811#issuecomment-1236270203"
    },
    {
      "author": "C0ffeeCode",
      "date": "2022-09-04",
      "body": "Can this also be used for scanning media for illegal/harmful/disturbing content?",
      "url": "https://github.com/matrix-org/matrix-spec-proposals/issues/3811#issuecomment-1236352589"
    },
    {
      "author": "m00nwtchr",
      "date": "2022-09-04",
      "body": "You'd need to use a technique like Neural Hash to create a database of content you want to block, but theoretically you could use this to implement the integration, afaict.",
      "url": "https://github.com/matrix-org/matrix-spec-proposals/issues/3811#issuecomment-1236409336"
    },
    {
      "author": "ndren",
      "date": "2022-09-17",
      "body": "Please make sure that this is documented that it must be always opt-in for E2EE attachments. It's important that this is up to explicit user choice, after they have considered their threat model. Thanks!",
      "url": "https://github.com/matrix-org/matrix-spec-proposals/issues/3811#issuecomment-1250013820"
    },
    {
      "author": "bxdxnn",
      "date": "2026-08-17",
      "body": "Element Pro implements this already as a content scanner.",
      "url": "https://github.com/matrix-org/matrix-spec-proposals/issues/3811#issuecomment-5318717802"
    }
  ],
