  "3944": [
    {
      "author": "bradtgmurray",
      "date": "2022-12-06",
      "body": "This looks great, and would help us out over at Beeper I think. We've been seeing clients (especially Element Web) generate a fair amount of room key chatter and mobile apps that aren't syncing actively at the time end up getting a large backlog of requests and cancellations when they do sync again. Since Synapse also limits the number of to_device events to 100 per response, this results in us having to do several syncs back-to-back until we can consider the app \"caught up\".",
      "url": "https://github.com/matrix-org/matrix-spec-proposals/pull/3944#issuecomment-1339983813"
    },
    {
      "author": "bradtgmurray",
      "date": "2026-01-25",
      "body": "From poking around, it seems like this was never implemented, is that correct? The tickets above got a little mangled in the migration from matrix-org/synapse to element-hq/synapse so it's not super clear what the state is. Is this MSC still relevant in a sliding-sync world?",
      "url": "https://github.com/matrix-org/matrix-spec-proposals/pull/3944#issuecomment-3795774944"
    },
    {
      "author": "kegsay",
      "date": "2026-01-26",
      "body": "Yes it's still relevant. It landed in the proxy but didn't land in the native Synapse implementation. ",
      "url": "https://github.com/matrix-org/matrix-spec-proposals/pull/3944#issuecomment-3798997111"
    }
  ],
  "3945": [
    {
      "author": "Zocker1999NET",
      "date": "2022-12-06",
      "body": "I like the idea of hiding the device names in the future as I agree with they are no longer required to be public thanks to cross-signing.\r\n\r\nHowever if others think public device names might still be useful to them, an easier idea could be that users can specify with a simple option if all their device names shall be public (which will be disabled by default). So techy aware users still can enable the option if required while knowing the risks. This would introduce less complexity than introducing separate public & private device names, especially because this does not require a change in the federation API, only in the client-server API.",
      "url": "https://github.com/matrix-org/matrix-spec-proposals/pull/3945#issuecomment-1340050764"
    },
    {
      "author": "uhoreg",
      "date": "2022-12-17",
      "body": "Apparently, I already wrote an MSC for the same thing: https://github.com/matrix-org/matrix-spec-proposals/pull/3480",
      "url": "https://github.com/matrix-org/matrix-spec-proposals/pull/3945#issuecomment-1356318836"
    }
  ],
  "3946": [
    {
      "author": "justjanne",
      "date": "2023-02-08",
      "body": "One desired use case with this is to allow users to view and access a predecessor room they haven't been in before, and which their homeserver likely doesn't know about.\r\n\r\n@t3chguy Just raised the issue with me that to join such rooms, the room id isn't enough, we'd also need the vias or a room alias. Which means the vias should be included at least in the dynamic predecessor message. As the static room predecessor message doesn't include vias either, use of that likely should be phased out.",
      "url": "https://github.com/matrix-org/matrix-spec-proposals/pull/3946#issuecomment-1422718038"
    },
    {
      "author": "nyabinary",
      "date": "2025-05-04",
      "body": "So whats the status of this?",
      "url": "https://github.com/matrix-org/matrix-spec-proposals/pull/3946#issuecomment-2848891715"
    }
  ],
