  "4021": [
    {
      "author": "bkil",
      "date": "2023-06-02",
      "body": "Neither MSC4021, nor MSC2291 copes with this to my liking.\r\n\r\nAs mentioned on matrix, I'd use more granular controls and it would be ideal to avoid the overloaded term `archiving`. I'd introduce the following levels in decreasing level of openness:\r\n\r\n- Redistributable (specify exact copyright/copyleft terms)\r\n- Allowed to process via statistical inference engines\r\n- Long term archiving/mirroring/backup with anonymization\r\n- Long term archiving/mirroring/backup (can store indefinitely and even versioned in systems such as MementoWeb, must document mechanism how a user can get their UGC removed from all such external archives),\r\n- Ephemerally short term cacheable by a search engines (i.e., for search result preview purposes)\r\n- Indexing and spidering allowed for search only\r\n- Specific hotlinks indexable for search only, but not allowed to spider - **default level during room creation**\r\n- Contextually hotlinkable preview while allowing for a bit of room chat context and interactive room browsing by humans (~statically rendered nojs client)\r\n- Hotlinkable preview (~unlisted individual messages),\r\n- For human eyes present in the room & over admin-authorized controlled bridges/relays\r\n- For present human eyes-only\r\n- ...\r\n",
      "url": "https://github.com/matrix-org/matrix-spec-proposals/pull/4021#issuecomment-1573936717"
    },
    {
      "author": "MadLittleMods",
      "date": "2023-06-02",
      "body": "@bkil Please use a thread off the diff for discussions and separate topics.",
      "url": "https://github.com/matrix-org/matrix-spec-proposals/pull/4021#issuecomment-1573962046"
    },
    {
      "author": "alphapapa",
      "date": "2023-06-04",
      "body": "IMHO this proposal is misguided, because a room with world-readable history can have its history read by any client, which would be free to ignore such \"controls.\"  That is, these would not be controls, but merely expressed preferences.  They would likely give users or room admins a false sense of security, because while they may have set a \"control\" to prevent indexing of their room's history, any party could be doing so with just a few lines of code, even connecting it to their own `archive.matrix.org`-like instance and feeding it to search engines.\r\n\r\nInstead, we should seek to make the consequences of room settings as clear as possible to users and admins.",
      "url": "https://github.com/matrix-org/matrix-spec-proposals/pull/4021#issuecomment-1575734525"
    }
  ],
