  "4048": [
    {
      "author": "chrkaatz",
      "date": "2025-03-07",
      "body": "May I ask for the progress and timeline for this topic? Is there a plan to have this implemented / finalized within the next couple of months?\r\n\r\nWe are facing an issue, that we shouldn't use libolm anymore in favor of vodozemac but need key backup as a hard requirement.",
      "url": "https://github.com/matrix-org/matrix-spec-proposals/pull/4048#issuecomment-2706121843"
    },
    {
      "author": "richvdh",
      "date": "2025-03-10",
      "body": "> May I ask for the progress and timeline for this topic? Is there a plan to have this implemented / finalized within the next couple of months?\r\n\r\nWe do hope to implement this in the medium term future, but it's not currently a focus for the Element team. \"Next couple of months\" is unlikely, I'm afraid.\r\n \r\n> We are facing an issue, that we shouldn't use libolm anymore in favor of vodozemac but need key backup as a hard requirement.\r\n\r\nI'm afraid I don't see the connection.",
      "url": "https://github.com/matrix-org/matrix-spec-proposals/pull/4048#issuecomment-2709688263"
    },
    {
      "author": "chrkaatz",
      "date": "2025-03-14",
      "body": "Of course, that connection is not easily visible. The Matrix protocol is used for one of Germany's healthcare digitalization efforts to enable communication between patients, healthcare professionals and even insurances. For that, there are specifications which defines the use of the matrix protocol and unfortunately, the agency responsible told us to switch to vodozemac in favor of megolm, but left open the issue regarding key backups even though the issue is known to them.",
      "url": "https://github.com/matrix-org/matrix-spec-proposals/pull/4048#issuecomment-2723871879"
    }
  ],
  "4049": [
    {
      "author": "andrewzhurov",
      "date": "2024-05-30",
      "body": "Sending as a \"Room\" sounds confusing to me. \"Room\" is [a rather unfortunate name](https://github.com/matrix-org/matrix-spec/issues/416#issuecomment-1055836830) for a Matrix Event Graph to begin with.\r\n\r\nWhat the described use-case wants, it seems, is to publish events from some sort of role _identifier_ (e.g., Acme corp) that may be collectively hold. E.g., top-level officers are authorized to publish announcements on behalf of Acme corp id.\r\n\r\nA way to manage such id in Self-Sovereign Identifier space is to e.g. use a MultiSig Autonomous Identifier (AID) of KERI.\r\nBasically, it states keys that need to sign in order for event to be deemed authentic.\r\nGiven we can have Profile Rooms #1769, such room is naturally a MultiSig AID, that could be used to manage authorized keys and add authenticity to actions on behalf of this ID. E.g., create an announcement event with one of the authorized keys and link to it from Profile Room to add authenticity. Or simply have a dedicated Announcements Room (with MultiSig requirement on it's events), a kind of Announcer ID of Acme corp.",
      "url": "https://github.com/matrix-org/matrix-spec-proposals/pull/4049#issuecomment-2138899407"
    }
  ],
