  "4226": [
    {
      "author": "deepadmax",
      "date": "2024-11-13",
      "body": "I imagine that a report room could be end-to-end encrypted; the subject may be sensitive. If that's the case, you may not want to store the *reason* unencrypted either. What if the reason would be stored elsewhere? A state event could refer to the event ID of the message to be used as the reason; by default, it would be the first message. Another benefit to storing it as state rather than in the creation event is that the reason can be changed later to better describe the problem.",
      "url": "https://github.com/matrix-org/matrix-spec-proposals/pull/4226#issuecomment-2474477010"
    }
  ],
  "4227": [
    {
      "author": "thoraj",
      "date": "2024-11-15",
      "body": "While I agree with goals of this MSC, I'm very doubtful it will work as specified. \r\n* the use of morse code seem strange. Since morse code was invented, there have been numerous innovation of more efficient ways to transmit information over audio channels  (FSK, DTMF or more advanced QAM methods) \r\n* the transmission must most likely use some form of error correcting code to get the desired accuracy\r\n* transmitting in the band 50khz-80khz (ultrasound) will be hard/impossible with standard phone hardware. Android samples at 44,1khz or 48khz afaik, which theoretically limits bandwidth to 22khz or 24khz (Nyquist limit)\r\n\r\nUsing more proven methods and protocols rather than inventing something new, seems more likely to succeed . ",
      "url": "https://github.com/matrix-org/matrix-spec-proposals/pull/4227#issuecomment-2479868303"
    },
    {
      "author": "albertotirla",
      "date": "2024-11-15",
      "body": "I will look more indepth at FSK, because this one seemns quite promising. The problem is, as always, if we have bindings for this protocol for at least as many programming languages as we have matrix sdks. I looked at something similar before, and the problem with all these is that we don't have enough bindings for this stuff as we have for qr code generation and scanning, which is probably even less than other methods.",
      "url": "https://github.com/matrix-org/matrix-spec-proposals/pull/4227#issuecomment-2479920752"
    }
  ],
