  "4357": [
    {
      "author": "Saiv46",
      "date": "2025-10-23",
      "body": "Shouldn't we use Sticky Events from MSC4354? It seems a perfect fit for live messages. Then on completion just send ordinary message without the edits.\r\n\r\nOtherwise users would hit into existing rate limits by constantly updating a single message.",
      "url": "https://github.com/matrix-org/matrix-spec-proposals/pull/4357#issuecomment-3438846274"
    },
    {
      "author": "toger5",
      "date": "2026-04-16",
      "body": "@Saiv46 Sticky events solve a different problem:\r\n - On sync I want to guarantee users download a specific event.\r\n \r\n This MSC seems to be targeted so that If I am already looking at an event i can see updates.\r\n Which does not need to be \"force synced\" if I dont look at the tile containing this \"update stack\" I am not interested in those events, so they can be fetched via a pull approach.\r\n \r\nSticky events are useful if you want a timeline item to (for at most 1h) have an impact on the room list **even for gappy syncs** where you are not yet actively viewing a room.\r\nLike for call participations.",
      "url": "https://github.com/matrix-org/matrix-spec-proposals/pull/4357#issuecomment-4260077400"
    }
  ],
