  "4443": [
    {
      "author": "thetayloredman",
      "date": "2026-04-01",
      "body": "Does this need a MSC? Updating permissions for spaces, the intended purpose, feels like a client feature. ",
      "url": "https://github.com/matrix-org/matrix-spec-proposals/pull/4443#issuecomment-4167049024"
    },
    {
      "author": "DidiDidi129",
      "date": "2026-04-01",
      "body": "> Does this need a MSC? Updating permissions for spaces, the intended purpose, feels like a client feature.\r\n\r\nI was thinking this could be handled by the client as if you were to edit the permissions from another client, it would cause a mis-match of permissions",
      "url": "https://github.com/matrix-org/matrix-spec-proposals/pull/4443#issuecomment-4167279298"
    },
    {
      "author": "thetayloredman",
      "date": "2026-04-01",
      "body": "> I was thinking this could be handled by the client as if you were to edit the permissions from another client, it would cause a mis-match of permissions\n\nIf I am understanding, the primary use case is spaces. In the same way that a client prompts if you want to leave rooms upon leaving a space, I don't see why it can't just be \"established convention\" to simply prompt if you want to propagate permission changes when making the changes in a parent space.\n\nThe use case between two actual chat rooms is intriguing though.",
      "url": "https://github.com/matrix-org/matrix-spec-proposals/pull/4443#issuecomment-4167288967"
    },
    {
      "author": "DidiDidi129",
      "date": "2026-04-01",
      "body": "> > I was thinking this could be handled by the client as if you were to edit the permissions from another client, it would cause a mis-match of permissions\n> \n> If I am understanding, the primary use case is spaces. In the same way that a client prompts if you want to leave rooms upon leaving a space, I don't see why it can't just be \"established convention\" to simply prompt if you want to propagate permission changes when making the changes in a parent space.\n> \n> The use case between two actual chat rooms is intriguing though.\n\nYou could have that except some clients won't support that\n\nI've never had a client ask me if I want to leave all the rooms part of a space before for example. ",
      "url": "https://github.com/matrix-org/matrix-spec-proposals/pull/4443#issuecomment-4169255184"
    },
    {
      "author": "uhoreg",
      "date": "2026-04-01",
      "body": "Given the lack of detail in this MSC, it is better to create an issue in https://github.com/matrix-org/matrix-spec/issues, work out the details there or elsewhere, and then write an MSC when things are more fleshed out.\r\n\r\nI'm going to close this for now.",
      "url": "https://github.com/matrix-org/matrix-spec-proposals/pull/4443#issuecomment-4170440887"
    }
  ],
