    {
      "author": "SpiritCroc",
      "date": "2026-04-09",
      "body": "Synapse PR / server implementation: https://github.com/element-hq/synapse/pull/19663",
      "url": "https://github.com/matrix-org/matrix-spec-proposals/pull/4446#issuecomment-4212325294"
    },
    {
      "author": "SpiritCroc",
      "date": "2026-04-09",
      "body": "[SchildiChat Revenge](https://github.com/SchildiChat/schildi-revenge/commit/00bc7924b8437d81bd24c6b4b41e467fa0b5702b) implements this via https://github.com/SchildiChat/matrix-rust-sdk/commit/e2d4ec21f513426d0f7e331dde7dc5abad77ba68 / https://github.com/SchildiChat/ruma/commit/54b2407c5cf60ca5732deeadb1533538777c37f6 (client side code already allowed picking any message for setting the fully read marker, so only SDK-side usage of the flag was needed).\r\n\r\nIn practice the client currently only invokes the `/receipt` endpoint for this purpose, not `/read_markers`. I don't have a strong opinion on whether both endpoints should allow the new flags, but figured for consistency it makes sense to allow for both, to support clients which may want to prefer `/read_markers` over `/receipt`.",
      "url": "https://github.com/matrix-org/matrix-spec-proposals/pull/4446#issuecomment-4215400663"
    }
